## Contents

### Files

* `Makefile` - main build and release targets to use locally; not used during CI

### Directories

* `terraform` - deployment configurations used during GCP CD execution via Terraform
* `terraform/local` - files used for local development only, won't be
  incorporated into the release artifact
* `terraform/tfvars` - tfvars files for all environments, including additional
  custom tfvars files
* `terraform/files` - miscellaneous files you may need to upload to
  Cloud Storage or use as templates
* `terraform/modules` - additional terraform modules
* `terraform/src` - sources for Cloud Functions, App Engine or similar services

## Develop locally

### Setup your laptop

```bash
# Set up you laptop for local development. Authenticate Google SDK and Initialize Terraform
make setup-laptop
```

After executing this target you will set up your Google SDK and Terraform.
Specifically you will authenticate to GCP and set up your default GCP Project,
region and zone.

### Terraform plan

```bash
# Build Terraform plan locally
make local-plan
```

Keep in mind that the state file is created locally on your hard drive.

### Terraform apply

```bash
# Deploy Terraform from your laptop
make local-deploy
```

Don't forget to destroy resources created with this target before scheduling a
CD Pipeline deployment as it may fail complaining on name conflicts.

### Terraform destroy

```bash
# Destroy resources previously created from your laptop
make local-destroy
```

This target will destroy any resource that is tracked in your locally stored
state file.

## Schedule deployments via CD Pipeline

### Release artifacts

```bash
# Upload Terraform artifact to Nexus repository to make it available for the CD Pipeline
make release
```

### Trigger promotion (artifact scan)

This step is optional for development but it's a good practice to perform a scan
to see what issues you may have in your artifact. Even if it fails you can move
forward with your Development deployment.
This step is mandatory



### Schedule deployment via Armada/SNOW/CD Pipeline

Deploy resources (assume `dev` for Terraform environment variable) from local machine

```bash
# deploys to Google Cloud assuming dev environment
make deploy

# deploys to a specified GCP Project
make deploy PROJECT_ID=....
```

### Destroy deployed resources

```bash
# destroys all resources
make deploy DEPLOY_ACTION=destroy
```
